            <div xml:id="d752">

                <pb facs="0998" n="884" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg884"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.34/213: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Morgan</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-01T18:00:00-05:00">December 1, 1931—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>92. Your 97, December 1, 11 a.m. The Department advised the Brazilian Ambassador
                    that in view of the provisions of Article 18 of the Washington Naval
                        Treaty<anchor n="7" xml:id="d752-f1"/> which provides that “each of the
                    Contracting Powers undertakes not to dispose by gift, sale or any mode of
                    transfer of any vessel of war in such a manner that such vessel may become a
                    vessel of war in the Navy of any foreign power”, this Government could not
                    comply with Brazil’s request to sell it two light fast cruisers. He was
                    furthermore informed that Article 11 of the London Naval Treaty<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d752-f2"/> provides that the rules for disposal contained in Annex 2
                    and Part 2 of the said Treaty shall be applied to all vessels of war to be
                    disposed of. The provisions regarding the removal of armaments and mutilation of
                    boilers, et cetera, set forth in section 5 of Annex 2 of the London Naval Treaty
                    regarding vessels retained for training purposes was also called to his
                    attention.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
